<ansi fg="black-bold">.:</ansi> <ansi fg="magenta">Help for </ansi><ansi fg="command">samurai</ansi>

The Samurai is a duelist who wins a fight in its first moment. It opens a
battle half a turn ahead of everyone else, its first strike hits harder and
crits more often, and it grows deadlier the longer no one lands a blow on it.
After that opening it is an ordinary front-line fighter in medium armor with
a good critical chance. It has no creed: no alignment gate stands in front of
any of its routes.

<ansi fg="yellow-bold">What the Samurai is</ansi>

  Health      6 to start, 0.85 a level to level 20 (<ansi fg="command">help health</ansi>)
  Skill       Attack 1.0 and Evasion 1.0 a level, like a warrior (<ansi fg="command">help evasion</ansi>)
  Gear        medium armor, no shield, swords only (<ansi fg="command">help armor</ansi>)
  Stats       speed 4, strength 3, perception 2, smarts 1 (<ansi fg="command">help growth</ansi>)
  Starter kit an iron shortsword, a padded jack, a leather cap, worn boots,
              food, a waterskin and a knapsack
  Utility     Camp Watch (<ansi fg="command">help campwatch</ansi>)

<ansi fg="yellow-bold">Ranks of the Samurai</ansi>

  Level 1   <ansi fg="yellow">Iaijutsu</ansi>  the Samurai starts every battle with half a turn on its action
            meter, so it acts sooner (<ansi fg="command">help tempo</ansi>). Its first strike of the battle
            deals 50% more damage with +10% critical chance. The strike is
            spent by that swing, hit or miss, and comes back with the next
            battle.
  Level 3   <ansi fg="yellow">Focus</ansi>     +3% critical chance for each round in a row in which no blow
            lands on the Samurai, up to +9%. A blow that lands resets it.
  Level 8   <ansi fg="yellow">Zanshin</ansi>   when the Samurai fells a foe, its action meter gains half a turn
            (once a round), so it is ready for the next one sooner.

Level 5 brings the first talent: Keen Edge, Footwork, Heavy Hands, Toughness
or Sharp Eye (+3% critical chance on every blow) (<ansi fg="command">help talents</ansi>). At level 10 a
Samurai promotes to a Kensai, Hatamoto or Ronin (<ansi fg="command">help samurai-routes</ansi>).

<ansi fg="yellow-bold">How a Samurai fights</ansi>

A battle plays out on its own, so everything above happens without a command.
A Samurai's default target rule is <ansi fg="command">strongest</ansi>: it goes for the foe with the most
health left, which is where a first strike counts most. <ansi fg="command">strategy me [rule]</ansi>
changes that (<ansi fg="command">help strategy</ansi>). Put it in the front or middle row (<ansi fg="command">help formation</ansi>);
Focus rewards a Samurai that is not the one being struck, so a guardian beside
it (<ansi fg="command">help guardian</ansi>) helps.

It may use only swords. The shipped swords are the iron shortsword, the steel
arming sword and the tempered sabre (<ansi fg="command">help equipmenttiers</ansi>).

<ansi fg="yellow-bold">Other Samurai</ansi>

A Samurai companion fights the same way, by its strategy, and promotes and
chooses talents like any other (<ansi fg="command">help company</ansi>). Recruits are hired like any
other and arrive with an iron shortsword.

Commands: <ansi fg="command">archetype</ansi>, <ansi fg="command">class</ansi>, <ansi fg="command">talent</ansi>, <ansi fg="command">strategy</ansi>.

See also: <ansi fg="command">help samurai-routes</ansi>, <ansi fg="command">help classes</ansi>, <ansi fg="command">help promotion</ansi>, <ansi fg="command">help talents</ansi>, <ansi fg="command">help archetype</ansi>, <ansi fg="command">help combat</ansi>.
